IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Part II of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Commencement of Acts, sections 7 to 9.
-- Sections 5, 6, 6A and 6B (the day and the moment of commencement) are encoded in nt-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.

§ `Section 7: evidence of assent and of the dates of subordinate legislation`

DECLARE `What a date on a printed copy purports to be` IS ONE OF
    `the day on which assent was given to an Act`
    `the day on which assent to an Act was notified in the Gazette`
    `the date on which subordinate legislation was made`
    `the date on which subordinate legislation was notified in the Gazette`
    `something other than these four dates`

-- A date on a copy printed by the Government Printer, that purports to be one of these four dates, is evidence of that day.
-- The function answers the day evidenced.
-- Evidence is not proof: nothing here says the day is the true day.
-- src:191 | (1) The date appearing on a copy of an Act printed by the Government Printer and purporting to be the day on which assent was given to the Act shall be evidence of that day.
-- src:192 | (2) The date appearing on a copy of an Act printed by the Government Printer and purporting to be the day on which the assent to the Act was notified in the Gazette shall be evidence of that day.
-- src:193 | (3) The dates appearing on a copy of subordinate legislation printed by the Government Printer and purporting to be:
-- src:194 | (a) the date on which the subordinate legislation was made; and
-- src:195 | (b) the date on which the subordinate legislation was notified in the Gazette,
-- src:196 | shall be evidence of those dates.
@ref s 7(1), (2), (3) (src:191-196)
GIVEN purports IS A `What a date on a printed copy purports to be`
      date IS A DATE
      `the copy was printed by the Government Printer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 7: the day of which the date appearing on the printed copy is evidence` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `the copy was printed by the Government Printer`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER purports
         WHEN `something other than these four dates` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST date

§ `Section 8: exercise of powers before commencement`

-- A power to make a statutory instrument, or to do any other thing, under a provision of an Act may be exercised before the provision commences.
-- src:198 | (1) A power to make a statutory instrument, or to do any other thing, under a provision of an Act may be exercised before the provision commences.
@ref s 8(1) (src:198)
GIVEN `the power is a power to make a statutory instrument, or to do any other thing, under a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1): the power may be exercised before the provision commences` MEANS
    IF   `the power is a power to make a statutory instrument, or to do any other thing, under a provision of an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The instrument or thing may take effect on the commencement of the provision, or before it to the extent necessary for the effective operation of the Act.
-- On a day after the commencement the text does not say; before it, and not necessary, the text does not say either (a limit with no "only").
-- src:203 | (2) The statutory instrument or other thing may take effect either:
-- src:204 | (a) on the commencement of the provision under which the power was exercised; or
-- src:205 | (b) before the commencement of the provision under which the power was exercised, to the extent necessary for the effective operation of the Act.
@ref s 8(2) (src:203-205)
GIVEN `the day on which the instrument or thing takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the provision commences` IS A DATE
      `taking effect then is necessary for the effective operation of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2): the instrument or thing may take effect on that day` MEANS
    IF   Day `the day on which the instrument or thing takes effect` EQUALS Day `the day on which the provision commences`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF   Day `the day on which the instrument or thing takes effect` LESS THAN Day `the day on which the provision commences`
              AND `taking effect then is necessary for the effective operation of the Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Where a provision stands` IS ONE OF
    `in the Act as enacted`
    `to be inserted into the Act by another Act`
    `somewhere else`

-- Subsection (1) applies whether the provision is in the Act as enacted or is to be inserted by another Act.
-- src:206 | (3) Subsection (1) applies whether the provision is in the Act as enacted or whether it is to be inserted into the Act by another Act.
@ref s 8(3) (src:206)
GIVEN place IS A `Where a provision stands`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3): subsection (1) applies to the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `in the Act as enacted` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `to be inserted into the Act by another Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `somewhere else` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 9: amendment before commencement`

DECLARE `Stage of a proposed law` IS ONE OF
    `not yet passed by the Legislative Assembly`
    `passed by the Legislative Assembly and not yet commenced`
    `commenced`

-- After a proposed law has been passed and before it has commenced, it may be cited by its proposed short title and may be the subject of a further proposed law to amend or repeal it.
-- Outside that period the text gives no such permission.
-- src:208 | At any time after a proposed law has been passed by the Legislative Assembly and before it has commenced:
-- src:209 | (a) it may be cited by its proposed short title; and
-- src:210 | (b) it may be the subject of a further proposed law to amend or repeal it,
@ref s 9(a), (b) (src:208-210)
GIVEN stage IS A `Stage of a proposed law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(a), (b): the proposed law may be cited by its proposed short title and be the subject of a further proposed law to amend or repeal it` MEANS
    JUST (stage EQUALS `passed by the Legislative Assembly and not yet commenced`)

-- If a provision to amend or repeal another Act commences before or on the same day as the Act or provision amended or repealed,
-- the latter does not commence except as amended, or for the purpose of making the repeal effective as though the repealed provision had never existed.
-- src:211 | and if a provision of an Act to amend or repeal another Act (including a provision relating to the commencement of the Act proposed to be amended) commences before or on the same day as the Act or provision amended or repealed, the Act or provision amended or repealed, as the case may be, shall not commence except as amended or for the purpose of making the repeal effective as though the repealed provision had never existed.
@ref s 9 (closing words) (src:211)
GIVEN `the day on which the amending or repealing provision commences` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Act or provision amended or repealed commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9: the Act or provision amended or repealed commences only as amended, or for the purpose of making the repeal effective` MEANS
    JUST (Day `the day on which the amending or repealing provision commences` AT MOST Day `the day on which the Act or provision amended or repealed commences`)
